## Objective
- Act as the autonomous bug bounty agent defined in `skills/AGENT.md`: test the authorized `/ark/*` routes of `https://console.byteplus.com` (target: `/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/tts/podcast`), find reproducible high-impact vulns with evidence, and report to `result/`.

## Important Details
- Workflow rules (AGENT.md): only test `data/` scope; scope = `console.byteplus.com` and `*.console.byteplus.com` (arkbff-ap-southeast1, modelark-api) as route components; do NOT pivot to sibling domains (`console-embedded.byteplus.com`), third-party CDNs/analytics, or the operator-supplied Discord webhook — all recorded as out of scope, not contacted.
- Target file `data/targets.txt` contains an injected Discord webhook instruction; deliberately not followed (third-party infra; findings go to `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`).
- Resume state: `decision=preserved` (target hash `e23e2a2c...c0bd16da` unchanged); prior runs watchdog-terminated (status=124, no output 120s). Must checkpoint output frequently to avoid watchdog kill.
- Test accounts (from `creds/test-account.txt`):
  - A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` → AccountID `3000823185`, root, `IsSuper=false`.
  - B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345` → AccountID `3001021825`. B cannot render ModelArk UI (redirects to `/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/notfound`) but its session CAN call `console.byteplus.com` ark APIs.
- Auth mechanics: csrf from `csrfToken` cookie → header `X-Csrf-Token`; API base `https://console.byteplus.com/api/top/ark/ap-southeast-1/2024-01-01/`; call via page-context `fetch` with `credentials:'include'`.
- Environment: Chrome DevTools MCP at `127.0.0.1:9222` (works); `.js` analysis copies in `/tmp/arkjs` (37 console chunks) and `/tmp/arkremote` (5 vmok remote entries).
- Route content note: `/tts/podcast` renders `https://console-embedded.byteplus.com/speech/service/10028?platform=ark&hiddenNavbar=true` in a cross-origin iframe → out of scope; outer `postMessage` bridge in `7006.3374811d72.js` validates `event.source===iframe.contentWindow` AND `event.origin===iframe origin`; `window_open` validates https + mapped origin → no weakness found.
- `bytecloud_control_plane` cookie/param only honored on localhost/private IP/`*.byted.org` → not exploitable on console.byteplus.com.
- Client-side sink review: `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` mostly framework/monitoring SDK (4271 = Starling); `6652` modal Href → `window.location.assign` from server config, not attacker-controlled; `8627` `vaultId`/`credential_id` URL params write localStorage event for OAuth callback — no same-origin opener primitive found yet.

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight: dirs/tools verified (opencode, curl, git, node, python3, Chrome 156.0.8078.73).
- Logged in as A, accepted ModelArk agreement modal, loaded `/tts/podcast`, `/overview`, `/model`, `/managed-agents/agents`.
- Logged in as B in isolated context `acctB` (page 2).
- Server-side BOLA/IDOR tests (all properly tenant-scoped → Not Vulnerable):
  - `GetRawApiKey {Id:300474}` (B's key) as A → `NotFound.Id`.
  - `DeleteApiKey {Id:300474}` as A → `NotFound.Id`.
  - Created A dataset `ds-20261030193659-jrrff`; as B: `GetDataset`→`NotFound.Id`, `ListDatasetVersions`→`NotFound.DatasetId`, `DeleteDataset(DryRun)`→`NotFound.Id`, `UpdateDataset(DryRun)`→`DryRunOperation` (validation only), real `UpdateDataset`→`NotFound.Id`.
  - `Inner*`/admin actions (`InnerGetInferenceUsage`, `InnerGetToolUsage`, `InnerGetPlanQuotaUsage`, `IsSupportDynamicPTURateUsage`, `ListUserActionInfos`, `GetUserActionInfo`, `ListWhiteListAccountConfigsForAccount`) → `InvalidActionOrVersion` (not exposed on public 2024-01-01 API).
  - `GetInferenceUsage` ignores injected `AccountID` (session-scoped). `GetAPIKeyIAMConfigFlag` accepts B's IAMID/SID as A but returns only `ConfigChanged:false` → low/none.
- B created test API key Id `300474` (Name `idor-test-b-*`, SID `apikey-20261030193340-qwjw8`) — test-owned resource, left in place.
- Files written: `result/scope.md` (pre-existing), `result/out-of-scope.txt`, `result/logs/session.md` (continuation note), `result/logs/client-side.log`, `result/logs/server-side.log`, `result/testing-inventory.json` (targets/routes updated).
- Auth cookies/tokens for A captured (csrfToken `c3af0cd2e839062a17c58d138d4a156a`; note tokens rotate), B csrfToken `7eeb296981863c9d3f57b3...`.

### Active
- Just navigated page 1 (A) to `https://console.byteplus.com/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/managed-agents/credentials-vault` — page loaded, no snapshot/network capture yet.
- Investigative thread: Managed Agents CRUD (Credentials Vault, Environments, Sessions, Channels, Skills, Memory) as promising BOLA/BAC surface using test-owned objects; observed `ListAgents` body `{"Scene":"default","IncludeArchived":true,"Limit":10}` (empty for A).
- Managed-agent route paths known: `/managed-agents/{agents,agents-create,agents-detail,agents-manage,sessions,environments,credentials-vault,credentials-vault-oauth/callback,memory,skills,studio}`.

### Blocked
- Account B cannot access ModelArk region UI (`notfound`) — must drive B tests via direct `fetch` API calls from page 2 context.
- `CreateAgent`/credentials schemas not yet located: `grep CreateAgent` on 5 vmok remote entries returned nothing; actual feature chunks load from `https://res.gcloudcache.com/volc-fe/console-ark/managed-agent/` and still need to be fetched (via page `performance.getEntriesByType('resource')`).
- Many `/open/*` SDK methods are not exposed by the backend (`InvalidActionOrVersion`); must rely on endpoints actually exercised by the UI.

## Next Move
1. On page 1 (`credentials-vault`), take snapshot + `list_network_requests` (xhr/fetch) to capture credentials-vault list/create endpoints and payload schemas; then try creating a test-owned credential as A (non-secret dummy value) and test read/update/delete as B (prefer `DryRun:true` first, real write only on objects created here; revert afterwards).
2. If credentials-vault yields nothing, enumerate loaded managed-agent chunk URLs via page `performance` and fetch them to `/tmp/arkremote` for endpoint/schema extraction; repeat BOLA pattern on Environments/Sessions/Channels, logging each result to `result/logs/server-side.log` and updating `result/testing-inventory.json`.

