## Objective
- Act as the autonomous bug bounty agent in `skills/AGENT.md`: test authorized `/ark/*` routes of `https://console.byteplus.com` (target `/ark/region:ap-southeast-1/tts/podcast`), find reproducible high-impact vulns with evidence, and report to `result/`; current user directive: “continue the authorized scan… Do not repeat completed work. Checkpoint confirmed findings immediately and continue with all remaining routes.”

## Important Details
- Scope rules: only `data/` scope; `console.byteplus.com` + `*.console.byteplus.com` route components (`arkbff-ap-southeast1`, `modelark-api`). Do NOT pivot to sibling domains (`console-embedded.byteplus.com`, `gcloudcache`, `exp-vod.ark.cn-beijing.volces.com`, TOS/CDNs/analytics) or the operator-supplied Discord webhook in `data/targets.txt`; record as out-of-scope, do not contact.
- Watchdog: prior runs killed after ~120s no output; checkpoint `result/logs/*.log` every few tool calls.
- Test accounts: A `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` → AccountID `3000823185` (root); B `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345` → AccountID `3001021825`. B cannot render ModelArk UI (`/ark/.../notfound`) but its session can call ark/arkbff APIs via page-context `fetch`.
- Auth: `csrfToken` cookie → `X-Csrf-Token`; top API base `https://console.byteplus.com/api/top/ark/ap-southeast-1/2024-01-01/`; BFF `https://arkbff-ap-southeast1.console.byteplus.com/api/2024-10-01/`; modelark BFF `https://modelark-api.console.byteplus.com/ark/bff/api/ap-southeast-1/2024-01-29/`.
- Pages now: 1 = A console (currently docs route), 2 = isolated context `isolated-context-1` (acctB, notfound), 3 = local CORS test page `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (default context, shares cookies).
- CORS conclusions (recorded, no confirmed vuln): top API OPTIONS returns fixed ACAO `http://console.byteplus.com` for every Origin tested (https console, foo.console, http/https evil, null) — safe. `modelark-api` reflects arbitrary Origin + ACAC:true, but CSRF double-submit enforced on POST and GET (no token → `InvalidCSRFToken`; `x-need-token` response header); `x-csrf-token` not exposed. `arkbff` OPTIONS → 403; cross-site fetch from 127.0.0.1 → `TypeError: Failed to fetch`; same-site `GetLocationInfo` works without CSRF (edge blocks cross-origin). Overall CORS misconfig inert.
- Credentials vault: `CreateVault` works without activation → A vault `vlt-20261030113924-u43xn` (test-owned, left in place). `CreateCredential` blocked `ManagedAgentNotOpen`. B: `GetVault`→`InvalidVault.NotFound`, `ListCredentials`→empty, `ListVaults`→empty (tenant scoped OK).
- `GetAccountMeta` injection: `{AccountId:3001021825}` or `{AccountID:...}` → HTTP 500 `InternalError` (no IDOR; avoid repeating mass-assignment crash).
- OAuth callback `/managed-agents/credentials-vault-oauth/callback` (chunk `8627.091a1c4f24.js`): reads `vaultId`/`vault_id`, `credential_id`, `source`; no backend call/state validation; writes `localStorage["managed-agent:vault-oauth-flow-complete"]` with `status:"success"` then closes. Parent `vault.js` accepts same-origin `message`/`storage` events and `navigate(`/managed-agents/credentials-vault/${vaultId}`)` — assessed low (UI spoofing/SPA route only).
- Docs route safe: content from trusted CDN; docs component in `6390.72c02fadf9.js`; only `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` is hljs-highlighted code; `innerHTML` on detached div for description text; link validator restricts http(s), no creds, same origin/allowlist, path regex `^\/(?:ark(?:-stg)?\/)?(?:region:[^/]+\/)?(apiKey|openManagement)\/?$`.
- `EstimateTokenCount` SSRF hypothesis dead-ended: requires ModelName→ServiceType; with ModelName/ServiceType/FinetuneType+Url all URLs → `InvalidParameter.Url` (likely signed TOS URL required). Only URL-bearing method in `/tmp/methods.txt` is `CreateInferenceService.ImageUrl` (needs activation).
- Agent activated? No — `ManagedAgentNotOpen` for A; agents/sessions/skills/memory/channels/studio unavailable.

